cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Same Question, Seven Engines: What Each AI Search Engine Cited — and Working Hypotheses for Targeting Each"
abstract: "One identical question, in English and Chinese, put to seven AI search surfaces on the same night; every cited URL captured, fetched, and classified by a frozen deterministic codebook. Reports cross-engine source overlap (domain-level Jaccard 0.171 CN / 0.091 EN), the page types engines actually cite, and the uptake of self-published ranked listicles. The offline half of the analysis is bit-reproducible: scripts/classify.py re-derives all 116 published page_type labels from the shipped per-page dossiers. v1.2 corrects four Cloudflare-blocked pages that were analysed from the interstitial rather than their recovered text; see ERRATUM.md."
